* ===========================================================================
* DOES CONTROL FLOW BUFFER UNDER DOTSCRIPT?  -- the reader-loop gap
* ===========================================================================
*
* A PROBE, NOT A REGISTERED SPEC. Not in kRegressionSpecs; runs by DOTSCRIPT.
*
* WHY. SCAN, LOOP, WHILE and UNTIL are LINE-CAPTURING constructs. The opening
* verb sets a flag; the READER LOOP then diverts every following line into a
* buffer until the closing verb executes it. That diversion is
* handle_buffers_if_active(), and it lives in the INTERACTIVE read loop --
* shell.cpp:695, immediately before shell_execute_line.
*
* cmd_dotscript.cpp:568 calls shell_execute_line DIRECTLY. There is no gate.
* So the prediction is: under DOTSCRIPT the opening verb flips the flag, the
* body lines execute IMMEDIATELY as ordinary commands, and the closing verb
* then iterates an EMPTY buffer.
*
* shell.cpp:398's own comment states the failure mode in advance:
*   "Otherwise loop/scan body lines leak through and execute once immediately
*    instead of being buffered."
*
* This probe asks whether that comment describes DOTSCRIPT today.
*
* WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT PROBED, AND WHY -- LOOP, WHILE, UNTIL.
* If their bodies leak, the closing verb iterates an empty buffer, so nothing
* in the body can ever change the escape condition. An inert loop may not
* TERMINATE. Hanging the session is an unacceptable way to measure this, so
* those three are left to a second probe with an externally bounded form.
* Their gate is the SAME ONE, so a SCAN result is evidence about them -- it is
* not proof, and this file does not claim it is.
*
* HOW IT ASSERTS. By FIELD VALUE, never console text. Both discriminators are
* built so that the LEAK PRODUCES A DIFFERENT VALUE rather than an absence,
* because an errored marker prints NOTHING rather than going red and an arm
* that can only vanish is not an arm.
*
* THE SCAN DISCRIMINATOR. The cursor is parked on record 1 before SCAN. If the
* body is buffered, every row is touched. If it leaks, the REPLACE runs ONCE
* against record 1 and no other row is touched. So:
*   T1 (record 1 touched)  -- passes EITHER WAY. It is a guard, not a verdict:
*                             it proves the REPLACE itself works.
*   T2 (record 4 touched)  -- THE DISCRIMINATOR. Buffered .T., leaked .F.
*
* THE IF DISCRIMINATOR. IF may not use this gate at all -- shell.cpp:405 refers
* to a separate "shell-level block capture" that runs AFTER it -- so IF is
* measured rather than assumed. If IF works, the THEN arm runs and M2 reads
* THEN. If IF leaks, BOTH branch bodies execute as ordinary lines and the
* second one wins, so M2 reads ELSE.
*   T3 -- THE DISCRIMINATOR. Working .T. (THEN), leaked reads ELSE.
*
* NOT A DISCRIMINATOR, stated so nobody adds it later thinking it is: an
* IF .F. case reads ELSE under BOTH implementations -- working IF takes the
* else branch, and a leak runs both and the else lands last. Identical output,
* zero information.
*
* COUNT: 2 guards + 3 arms = 5 DSC_ lines. An errored marker prints NOTHING,
* so A SHORT COUNT IS ITSELF THE RESULT. Read the count before the values.
*
* Self-bootstrapping and self-erasing in DBF/SANDBOX. Read-only with respect
* to everything else; mints no catalog rows and opens no workspace.
* ===========================================================================

SETPATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX

ERASE DSCTL CONFIRM

SELECT 0
CREATE X64 DSCTL (CK C(4), M1 C(8), M2 C(8))
APPEND
REPLACE CK WITH "C1"
REPLACE M1 WITH "ZERO"
REPLACE M2 WITH "ZERO"
APPEND
REPLACE CK WITH "C2"
REPLACE M1 WITH "ZERO"
REPLACE M2 WITH "ZERO"
APPEND
REPLACE CK WITH "C3"
REPLACE M1 WITH "ZERO"
REPLACE M2 WITH "ZERO"
APPEND
REPLACE CK WITH "C4"
REPLACE M1 WITH "ZERO"
REPLACE M2 WITH "ZERO"

USE DSCTL
SELECT DSCTL

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* GUARDS -- the fixture, and that a bare REPLACE works at all
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GO 4
? "DSC_G1_fixture_row4_is_C4:" + (ALLTRIM(CK) = "C4")

GO 2
REPLACE M1 WITH "BARE"
GO 2
? "DSC_G2_bare_replace_outside_a_block_works:" + (ALLTRIM(M1) = "BARE")

GO 2
REPLACE M1 WITH "ZERO"

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE SCAN ARM -- park on record 1 first, so a leak is confined to record 1
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GO 1
SCAN
REPLACE M1 WITH "HIT"
ENDSCAN

GO 1
? "DSC_T1_scan_record1_touched_GUARD_NOT_VERDICT:" + (ALLTRIM(M1) = "HIT")
GO 4
? "DSC_T2_scan_record4_touched_DISCRIMINATOR:" + (ALLTRIM(M1) = "HIT")

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE IF ARM -- a leak runs BOTH bodies and the ELSE lands last
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GO 1
IF .T.
REPLACE M2 WITH "THEN"
ELSE
REPLACE M2 WITH "ELSE"
ENDIF

GO 1
? "DSC_T3_if_then_branch_taken_DISCRIMINATOR:" + (ALLTRIM(M2) = "THEN")
